# Both images build from the repository root (atlas/api/Dockerfile,
# atlas/web/Dockerfile), and `fly deploy` uploads the build context to a
# remote builder — so the context is deny-by-default: nothing leaves this
# machine but what the two Dockerfiles copy. Never the data, the results,
# private files, key files or the decision records' packets (Phase 4).
*
!requirements.lock
!atlas/__init__.py
!atlas/api/
!atlas/model/
!atlas/docs/methodology.md
!atlas/docs/crime.md
!atlas/docs/privacy.md
!atlas/web/
atlas/model/tests/
atlas/api/tests/
atlas/web/node_modules/
atlas/web/.next*/
atlas/web/content/
atlas/web/test-results/
atlas/web/playwright-report/
atlas/web/e2e/
atlas/web/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/.DS_Store
